=== RRQ: my derived expected content ===
RRQ1 Invisible/elastic parts of the job land on whoever absorbs them; a conscientious
     teacher absorbs more than a disengaged one. topic-01.
RRQ2 Stress = response to demands exceeding resources in the moment; episodic; resolves.
     Burnout = product of chronic unresolved demand; three dimensions = exhaustion,
     cynicism/depersonalisation, reduced personal accomplishment/efficacy.
     "Where each of this unit's two burnout sources was conducted":
       Skaalvik & Skaalvik 2020 = Norway, high schools, 262 teachers. ANSWERABLE.
       Maslach & Leiter 2016 = the unit describes it as a REVIEW across human-service
       occupations, health care in particular, expressly "not about teachers". A review
       has no conduct site, and the unit supplies none.
     >>> The item's stem presupposes a location for BOTH sources. The unit supports a
         location for one. Flagged as an item defect, derived blind.
RRQ3 Physical, Human, Instructional, Structural; last two (instructional, structural)
     underestimated because the absence of e.g. anyone to ask about a non-decoding Class 4
     pupil is not discussed and converts a solvable problem into a permanent one. topic-01.
RRQ4 Any two of: what is measured becomes what is done; effort moves from the work to the
     record of the work; compliance/managed exposure rather than improvement. topic-02.
RRQ5 Any three of pupils/parents/head/district/examination system/public, wants vs measures
     as bulleted in topic-02.
RRQ6 Status = society's standing for the occupation (pay, entry, autonomy, how spoken of);
     recognition = what a particular community extends to the teachers it deals with.
     Follows: the belief is false of recognition even where true of structural status.
RRQ7 Three questions: what does it add that was not possible before; what does it cost
     (money, time, set-up, failure, training, attention); what does it replace that was
     already working.
     >>> The stem asks why the third is "the hardest to answer HONESTLY". The unit says it
         is the question "nobody asks" / "most often missed". Not the same property; the
         honesty framing must be inferred. Minor stem/text drift, recorded.
RRQ8 Two of: pupils without a phone are excluded from what is announced there; the group
     runs at all hours so expected availability expands without anyone deciding it;
     a message sent in haste is permanent and forwardable.
RRQ9 Control / influence / do not control, with topic-04's examples.
RRQ10 Without deciding evidence in advance "you will conclude whatever you hoped".
     Unit asserts it is most often skipped but does not state WHY; the why must be reasoned
     (it costs effort up front and forecloses a comfortable verdict). Analyze label is apt.

